      "id": 1,
      "text": "Little Falls grew around the waterfalls on the Mississippi River, and the town’s name comes directly from those falls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Falls%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was founded in 1891 by the Franciscan Sisters of the Immaculate Conception, who established a Catholic community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Falls%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Multiple dams were constructed over Little Falls’ waterfalls in the 1800s, providing power for sawmills that drove early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Falls%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Lindbergh Historic Site in Little Falls houses Charles Lindbergh’s boyhood home, a visitor center, and a full‑scale flight simulator.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
